    <briefdescription>
<para>Generic temporal filter with confidence-scaled convergence and smoothstep S-curve dropout decay. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Designed for signals that require smooth tracking during active sampling and graceful, non-penalizing decay during brief dropouts (e.g. tracking priors, orientation hints).</para>
<para>Dual-regime dynamics:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Active Sampling (has_sample == true): Filters values with exponential smoothing whose effective time constant scales inversely with confidence: tau_eff = base_tau_track / confidence. High confidence gives rapid convergence; low confidence dampens jitter.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Dropout Decay (has_sample == false): Holds the last valid state over a configurable grace window (hold_window_s) with zero initial rate of change (w&apos;(0) = 0). Beyond the hold window, smoothly accelerates and decelerates decay towards the neutral baseline along a cubic Hermite smoothstep S-curve (w(t) = 1 - 3t^2 + 2t^3) over decay_window_s. </para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
